  "description": "NEKBEN crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H86 Dy8 N52 Ni6 O38 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),7(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 0 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 1 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1A (Ni) has 2 O neighbors; Ni2A (Ni) has 0 O neighbors; Ni3A (Ni) has 1 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.499-4.065 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.25-128.19°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C79H114Dy8Ni6N54O51. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
